A||||8||Rodney||Rear deck lid strap kits for R&D||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||08-05-2001||11:22 AM||||Anyone have broken rear deck lid straps? Looking for someone to try out a free pair of the plated eyelet end straps. You can install them with the hinges still installed in your car as these are the type that require you to drill and tap the hole the factory rivit was in. You will need a .257 drill bit and a 5/16" x 18 tap. When I start to offer these I'll have on my web page this drill and tap for about $5.00 extra for those who do not have them on hand. Having a digital camera would be a plus! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||08-05-2001||12:19 PM||||Guess you will have to excuse my ignorance again. My straps are broken,(cut actually) but I never gave it much thought, what is the purpose for them? You're gonna sell a drill & tap for $5? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Don<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||1
